{"total_count":479517,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208","id":5645368021,"node_id":"I_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAABUH161Q","number":208,"title":"Add public API compatibility fixtures and breaking-change gates","user":{"login":"Aboyeji-Isaac","id":141873116,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHTP3A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141873116?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac","html_url":"https://github.com/Aboyeji-Isaac","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aboyeji-Isaac/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11821061066,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAACwJcTyg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11821061075,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAACwJcT0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12310648705,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAAC3cWXgQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/labels/complexity:%20high","name":"complexity: high","color":"EF4444","default":false,"description":"Requires real verification work or judgment calls. ~200 pts","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12310649191,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAAC3cWZZw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/labels/drips-wave","name":"drips-wave","color":"6366F1","default":false,"description":"Open for Stellar Drips Wave contribution and points","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12311066164,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT3R9oc8AAAAC3cv2NA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/labels/Stellar%20Wave","name":"Stellar Wave","color":"5555ff","default":false,"description":"Issues in the Stellar wave program","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"emarkees","id":85732251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzMyMjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85732251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees","html_url":"https://github.com/emarkees","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2026-09-30T10:59:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T11:22:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"emarkees","id":85732251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzMyMjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85732251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees","html_url":"https://github.com/emarkees","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emarkees/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\nAdd executable compatibility contracts for StellarCore's public APIs so accidental response-shape or semantic breaking changes are caught before merge or deployment.\n\n## Current State\nAudited main: `973cf2821f3499ae41d65d5806ba539c3b35f237`.\n\nThe repository has route-level tests and API types, but there is no versioned compatibility fixture set that defines which response fields, nullability rules, status codes, and evidence-state semantics existing clients may rely on.\n\n## What to Build\n- Capture canonical fixtures for representative successful and error responses across anchors, corridors, rates, and reputation.\n- Define which changes are backward-compatible versus breaking.\n- Add CI checks that compare current serializers against the compatibility contract.\n- Allow intentional breaking changes only through an explicit reviewed update process.\n- Normalize nondeterministic fields before comparison without hiding meaningful changes.\n- Document deprecation/migration expectations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Existing representative responses are covered by canonical fixtures.\n- [ ] Removing/renaming required fields fails the compatibility gate.\n- [ ] Compatible additive changes follow a documented policy.\n- [ ] Error/status-code regressions are detected.\n- [ ] Timestamp/order normalization does not mask semantic changes.\n- [ ] Intentional contract updates require explicit fixture changes and review.\n- [ ] Typecheck, lint, targeted tests, full tests, and build pass.\n\n## Dependencies / Out of Scope\n#177 standardizes error envelopes and #25 documents the API. This issue owns executable backward-compatibility enforcement.\n\n## Complexity\nHigh — 200 points. Requires formal compatibility rules, deterministic serialization, multi-endpoint fixtures, CI gating, and a safe intentional-change workflow.\n\n## Contributor Coordination\nJoin the StellarCore Telegram group: https://t.me/+Go1LGH00JNg2OGE0\n\nUse the issue thread for implementation-specific design decisions, verification evidence, and maintainer review so important technical context remains recorded on GitHub.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aboyeji-Isaac/StellarCore/issues/208/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307","id":5114242689,"node_id":"I_kwDORYtWxs8AAAABMNUmgQ","number":307,"title":"Introduce a backward compatibility layer","user":{"login":"vriesdemichael","id":9072548,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzI1NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9072548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael","html_url":"https://github.com/vriesdemichael","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12000423165,"node_id":"LA_kwDORYtWxs8AAAACy0fs_Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/labels/predictable%20behavior","name":"predictable behavior","color":"630da7","default":false,"description":"Improves predictability for users (also for unexpected behavior that isnt a bug)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12116748521,"node_id":"LA_kwDORYtWxs8AAAAC0jbo6Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/labels/staged%20on%20next","name":"staged on next","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issue is already implemented on the next branch and will ship with the next release","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/milestones/2","html_url":"https://github.com/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/milestone/2","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/milestones/2/labels","id":17751204,"node_id":"MI_kwDORYtWxs4BDtyk","number":2,"title":"v5.0.0","description":"Work planned for the next major release.\n\nTwo ways in. A change is admitted automatically when its fix must carry a breaking marker under ADR-066: it alters an exit code, an error kind, a flag's meaning or the shape of parsed output, or it rejects an invocation that previously succeeded. Restoring behaviour an accepted ADR or a shipped release note already promised is a fix, not a break, and does not belong here.\n\nLarge additive work is admitted by decision instead, when a major is the sensible place to land it.\n\nNothing releases from the next branch, so this milestone is a plan rather than a queue; ADR-066 has how the work integrates.","creator":{"login":"vriesdemichael","id":9072548,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzI1NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9072548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael","html_url":"https://github.com/vriesdemichael","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vriesdemichael/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":27,"closed_issues":3,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-09-09T09:20:13Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T20:18:11Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-10T20:50:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T06:11:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Atlassian makes breaking changes to their api at their whim. This project has tests to verify it still works with the CI version (pinned at a maximum as well for now)\n\nTo properly make this tool work out of the box, even for sluggish enterprises with an update pace that puts them behind the breaking changes this tool should support a range of versions, ensuring that all calls either get translated to their versioned implementation or display a proper error.\n\nThis would also need proper breaking change tracking and testing against all supported versions in the CI as well.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vriesdemichael/bitbucket-data-center-cli/issues/307/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248/events","html_url":"https://github.com/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248","id":5620341067,"node_id":"I_kwDOCEtbgs8AAAABTv-ZSw","number":11248,"title":"Breaking server and sdk compatibility too often","user":{"login":"JWCS","id":10385237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzg1MjM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10385237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS","html_url":"https://github.com/JWCS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JWCS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":979236953,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NzkyMzY5NTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2803643685,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODAzNjQzNjg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/labels/need%20info","name":"need info","color":"E2C32B","default":false,"description":"Need more information to investigate the issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:53:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T03:25:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Actions before raising this issue\n\n- [x] I searched the existing issues and did not find anything similar.\n- [x] I read/searched [the docs](https://docs.cvat.ai/docs/)\n\n### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nIn our prod tooling integrating with cvat, more than any other resource, library, or tooling, only cvat sdk+server go through so much frequent breakage.\nOur unit tests are constantly getting spammed with \"this version is not compatible anymore\".\nWhen our usage of cvat doesn't change, when we're not doing anything new with it, we're still getting spammed.\nThis isn't a young project anymore; can we get some api stability? \nThere's no meaningful semver, there's no breakage warning, no depr warnings, no indications of what version bumps matter or don't matter.\nWe don't want to have to babysit our cvat cli versions. This has already bit us when overnight a minor version bump completely broke our pipelines.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\nIdeally, that cvat's APIs are stable enough or backwards compatible enough that we only need to upgrade as-needed, or for rare overhauls.\n\nAdditionally, using semver meaningfully to indicate actual breaking behavior, and depr warnings on versions before that, so we have better awareness of the risks of not upgrading, and to know what to prioritize.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\n\nWe just have more defensive tooling enabled, to warn us when cvat's sdk breaks our stuff. \n\nIt's also risky to upgrade, because we don't know if upgrading will break our usage; when we're not changing our usage, we don't want to waste time on cvat's release cadence validating if what we were doing is now broken. It releases too often for us to do this constantly. \n\n### Additional context\n\nThis isn't meant to be mean, but it is a painful gap, that only exists for us while using cvat. \nOur tools work with multiple cvat servers (tho mostly your main), so we don't have the luxury of freezing a server version. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cvat-ai/cvat/issues/11248/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}